⚠️ THIS IS A TEMPORARY LICENSE, NOT OUR FINAL LICENSE ⚠️

Georama is intended to become open source. We have not yet decided
which open-source license best fits the project, and we did not want that
decision to delay letting the community see, test, and give feedback on
the current state of the code.

Rather than provisionally applying an open-source license now — which
could unintentionally lock us into terms that limit our choice of final
license later — we are temporarily releasing this code under the
restrictive terms below. This is a deliberate, short-term trade-off: we
believe it is more valuable for people to be able to inspect and try the
software today than to wait until the licensing question is fully
resolved.

We expect to replace this license with a permanent open-source license
by the beginning of 2027 (tentative). Once that happens, this temporary
license will no longer apply, and the project will be governed by the
new open-source license going forward.

